# Batshit Docker Environment Example
# Copy this file to .env.docker before running:
#   cp .env.docker.example .env.docker
#   ./start-docker.sh
# On Windows PowerShell, use:
#   node tools/docker/start-docker.mjs
#
# The launcher can generate stable local secrets when placeholders are still
# present, prepares the built-in Docker Sandbox operator, and then runs Docker
# Compose. You can also replace the placeholder secrets yourself before first
# launch. Direct `docker compose --env-file .env.docker ...` remains available
# for advanced/debug use after the env file has been prepared.

# Required: keep these stable after first boot.
# If replacing them yourself, one easy local option is:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
BATSHIT_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-token
ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-a-long-stable-secret-at-least-32-chars

# Optional host-port and browser URL overrides. These are read by Docker Compose
# when you run with `docker compose --env-file .env.docker ...`.
#
# SECURITY: published ports bind to 127.0.0.1 by default, so only the machine
# running Docker can reach Batshit. Setting BATSHIT_DOCKER_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0
# exposes the Batshit app login page AND batshit-server to every device on
# your network — only do that on a network you trust, and know that anyone on
# it can reach those ports. Update the browser URLs below to a host-reachable
# address if you do.
BATSHIT_DOCKER_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
BATSHIT_DOCKER_APP_PORT=5620
BATSHIT_DOCKER_SERVER_PORT=5600
# If you enable the optional Docker n8n profile and already run n8n on the host
# at 5678, change this to another host port such as 5679. Also update the
# host-facing n8n URLs below to the same host port. For side-by-side local
# testing with another n8n on localhost, use 127.0.0.1 for the optional profile's
# browser-facing URLs so the two n8n auth cookies do not collide.
BATSHIT_DOCKER_N8N_PORT=5678
ORIGIN=http://localhost:5620
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5620
PUBLIC_BATSHIT_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:5600
PUBLIC_BATSHIT_SERVER_API_URL=http://localhost:5600/api/v1

# In-app update notices. Defaults track the packaged alpha release; leave the
# override fields blank unless testing a notice or using a custom release feed.
BATSHIT_APP_VERSION=0.1.0-alpha.1
BATSHIT_APP_CHANNEL=alpha
BATSHIT_UPDATE_CHECK_DISABLED=0
BATSHIT_UPDATE_FEED_URL=
BATSHIT_UPDATE_LATEST_VERSION=
BATSHIT_UPDATE_RELEASE_URL=
BATSHIT_UPDATE_DOWNLOAD_URL=

# Optional advanced override. Leave blank for Docker's internal app URL.
BATSHIT_ARTIFACT_COMPLETE_URL=
# Leave blank for automatic behavior: http://localhost uses non-secure cookies,
# https origins use secure cookies. Set to true/false only for a deliberate proxy setup.
BATSHIT_SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=
# Docker gets its own localhost cookie name so it can stay logged in beside
# other local Batshit instances without overwriting their sessions.
BATSHIT_SESSION_COOKIE_NAME=batshit_session_docker
# SvelteKit adapter-node request body limit for Admin backup restore and large uploads.
# The default supports multi-hundred-MB Goon imports while still keeping a
# bounded app-container request cap. Raise only if the host has enough memory.
BODY_SIZE_LIMIT=1G

# Optional Codex / Claude CLI integration.
# The Docker app image does not bundle Codex or Claude Code. To use CLI agents,
# start the stack, open the CLI agent in Settings, use the one-click install
# card, then run the Docker-aware login command Batshit shows. For a managed
# Codex install, it usually looks like:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker exec app /home/batshit-cli/.batshit/installs/cli/bin/codex login --device-auth
# Claude login commands include `exec --user batshit-cli ...` so Claude Code
# auth/status/runs use the same non-root HOME that supports Bypass Permissions.
# Add `--profile n8n` before `exec` when the stack was started with that profile.
# /workspace is the default Docker work directory.
BATSHIT_CODEX_PROVIDER_ENABLED=true
BATSHIT_CODEX_WORKDIR=/workspace
# Project workspace mount. `./start-docker.sh` fills this with the current
# checkout path when it is blank so Project file trees, CLI/Codex agents, and
# Docker Sandbox all see the same files through /workspace. Set it yourself
# before launch when Batshit should use a different host folder.
BATSHIT_WORKSPACE_MOUNT=

# Optional Docker MCP Gateway/controller. Leave blank unless you intentionally
# run a separate Docker MCP Gateway or host-side controller for Docker-backed
# tools. For a gateway running on the host, set DOCKER_MCP_GATEWAY_PORT or use
# a container-reachable URL such as http://host.docker.internal:5608.
MCP_GATEWAY_AUTH_TOKEN=
DOCKER_MCP_GATEWAY_URL=
DOCKER_MCP_GATEWAY_PORT=
DOCKER_MCP_PROFILE=

# Optional managed Cloudflared sidecar for local Clip tunnel URLs.
# The default Batshit Docker stack does not include this sidecar. To enable it:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile cloudflared up -d --build
# The sidecar writes its current trycloudflare URL into a shared runtime volume
# so Batshit can resolve local clip URLs without the core app container owning
# Docker itself. The target is a Compose-internal URL in Docker mode; the
# `5600` below is the batshit-server container port, not a host localhost port.
CLOUDFLARED_RELEASE_TAG=2026.3.0
CLOUDFLARED_LINUX_AMD64_SHA256=4a9e50e6d6d798e90fcd01933151a90bf7edd99a0a55c28ad18f2e16263a5c30
CLOUDFLARED_LINUX_ARM64_SHA256=0755ba4cbab59980e6148367fcf53a8f3ec85a97deefd63c2420cf7850769bee
BATSHIT_CLOUDFLARED_TARGET_URL=http://batshit-server:5600
BATSHIT_CLOUDFLARED_METRICS=0.0.0.0:20241
BATSHIT_CLOUDFLARED_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS=15

# First-party host-side runtime add-on operator.
# `./start-docker.sh` fills these with the same local operator used by Docker
# Sandbox, so Admin buttons and permissioned agents can start/stop approved
# Docker sidecars such as FBX-to-VRMA. The operator maps known add-on IDs/actions
# to hardcoded Compose behavior; it does not accept arbitrary shell commands
# from Batshit. If you intentionally bypass the launcher, leave these blank to
# show manual Compose commands instead of start/stop buttons.
BATSHIT_RUNTIME_ADDON_OPERATOR_URL=
BATSHIT_RUNTIME_ADDON_OPERATOR_TOKEN=
BATSHIT_RUNTIME_ADDON_OPERATOR_TIMEOUT_MS=180000

# Docker Sandbox is Batshit's built-in isolated agent sandbox. In Docker
# installs the core app container still does not get the host Docker socket, so
# Sandbox uses Batshit's first-party host operator. `./start-docker.sh`
# generates the token, fills the URL/workspace mapping, and starts that
# operator before Compose so Agent Mode has its sandbox available by default.
#
# If you intentionally bypass the launcher and run raw Docker Compose, fill
# these values yourself and run `node tools/docker/runtime-addon-operator.mjs`
# on the host before using Sandbox-backed agent actions.
#
# The operator reads .env.docker by default, exposes /v1/sandbox/*, translates
# /workspace to the host mount, applies deny-network policy, and never gives the
# app container direct host Docker control.
BATSHIT_NATIVE_DOCKER_SANDBOX_DRIVER=operator
BATSHIT_DOCKER_SANDBOX_OPERATOR_URL=
BATSHIT_DOCKER_SANDBOX_OPERATOR_TOKEN=
BATSHIT_DOCKER_SANDBOX_OPERATOR_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
BATSHIT_SANDBOX_CONTAINER_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/workspace
BATSHIT_SANDBOX_HOST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=

# Optional FBX-to-VRMA worker sidecar for Goon Motion Vault FBX uploads.
# The default Batshit Docker stack does not include this worker. To enable it:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile fbx2vrma up -d --build fbx2vrma-worker
# The app calls this service over the Compose network when an .fbx animation is
# uploaded. Native Mac/Windows/Linux binary install buttons stay disabled in Docker.
# FBX2glTF only publishes a Linux x64 binary, so the worker runs as linux/amd64
# even on Apple Silicon Docker Desktop.
FBX2GLTF_VERSION=v0.9.7
FBX2GLTF_LINUX_X64_SHA256=b38210352fdd29d50ba53a6514c3ff05ccbb5d1e0a6442db7a49834bf34a3145
BATSHIT_FBX2VRMA_WORKER_URL=http://fbx2vrma-worker:8079
BATSHIT_FBX2VRMA_MAX_BYTES=524288000
BATSHIT_FBX2VRMA_CONVERT_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Optional Batshit Audio2Face bridge for premium completed-utterance face
# animation. This profile starts only Batshit's open bridge; it does not bundle,
# download, license, or start NVIDIA Audio2Face-3D NIM. Start a licensed NIM
# v2.0 runtime separately (normally on an NVIDIA GPU host at port 52000), accept
# NVIDIA's applicable terms, then enable the bridge with:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile audio2face up -d --build audio2face-bridge
# `./start-docker.sh` generates the bridge token. Raw Compose users must set one.
NVIDIA_A2F_SAMPLES_COMMIT=a2d0150043be7dc15db2fad8193a78b660e1100f
NVIDIA_A2F_SAMPLES_SHA256=827b47831b1640b8bffef005a2a07eb58bc793894e331638253b3080e628ab27
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_BRIDGE_URL=http://audio2face-bridge:8068
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_BRIDGE_TOKEN=
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_ENDPOINT=host.docker.internal:52000
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_TLS=0
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_ROOT_CERT=
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_CLIENT_CERT=
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_CLIENT_KEY=
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_NIM_HEALTH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_MAX_AUDIO_BYTES=67108864
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_CACHE_MAX_BYTES=2147483648
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=2000
BATSHIT_AUDIO2FACE_TONGUE_ENABLED=0

# Optional Agent Browser sidecar for browser automation from Docker Batshit.
# The default core Docker stack does not include a browser runtime. To enable it:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile agent-browser up -d --build agent-browser
# `./start-docker.sh` fills the sidecar URL/token automatically. The sidecar
# runs the pinned Agent Browser CLI and a local headless browser inside Docker;
# it does not use your host Chrome profile, cookies, or display.
AGENT_BROWSER_VERSION=0.24.1
BATSHIT_AGENT_BROWSER_SIDECAR_URL=http://agent-browser:8091
BATSHIT_AGENT_BROWSER_SIDECAR_TOKEN=
BATSHIT_AGENT_BROWSER_TMP_DIR=/runtime/agent-browser/tmp

# Optional LiveKit voice runtime add-on for LiveKit-backed Voice Mode.
# LiveKit is a runtime, not a TTS/STT engine. To enable the local Docker
# runtime:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile livekit up -d --build livekit livekit-agent
# The browser connects to LIVEKIT_URL, while the Docker app uses
# LIVEKIT_INTERNAL_URL for server-side agent dispatch. Keep these in sync with
# BATSHIT_DOCKER_LIVEKIT_PORT if you change the published LiveKit port.
LIVEKIT_SERVER_IMAGE=livekit/livekit-server:v1.12.0
BATSHIT_DOCKER_LIVEKIT_PORT=7880
BATSHIT_DOCKER_LIVEKIT_RTC_TCP_PORT=7881
BATSHIT_DOCKER_LIVEKIT_RTC_UDP_PORT=7882
LIVEKIT_URL=ws://localhost:7880
LIVEKIT_INTERNAL_URL=ws://host.docker.internal:7880
LIVEKIT_AGENT_LIVEKIT_URL=ws://livekit:7880
LIVEKIT_AGENT_HEALTH_URL=http://livekit-agent:7899/worker
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=batshit-local
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=replace-with-livekit-local-secret
LIVEKIT_VOICE_AGENT_NAME=batshit-livekit-agent
LIVEKIT_AGENT_MODE=batshit-bridge
LIVEKIT_AGENT_BATSHIT_BASE_URL=http://app:3000
LIVEKIT_AGENT_BATSHIT_TOKEN=

# Optional ComfyUI-shaped validation sidecar for artifact runtime checks.
# This is not a full GPU ComfyUI distribution. To enable the validation sidecar:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker --profile comfyui-validation up -d --build comfyui-validation
BATSHIT_COMFYUI_VALIDATION_URL=http://comfyui:8188
BATSHIT_DOCKER_COMFYUI_VALIDATION_PORT=8188

# AI provider API keys are optional here because they can be saved in Settings -> API Keys.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
MINIMAX_API_KEY=
MIMO_API_KEY=
ALIBABA_CLOUD_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
STEPFUN_API_KEY=
STEP_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
ZAI_API_KEY=
ZAI_CODING_API_KEY=
DEEPINFRA_API_KEY=
TOGETHER_API_KEY=
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
BASETEN_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# Optional OpenAI-compatible base URL overrides.
# MOONSHOT_API_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1
# MINIMAX_API_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/v1
# MIMO_API_BASE_URL=https://api.xiaomimimo.com/v1
# ALIBABA_CLOUD_API_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# DASHSCOPE_API_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# ALIBABA_CLOUD_TTS_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/api/v1
# DASHSCOPE_TTS_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/api/v1
# STEPFUN_API_BASE_URL=https://api.stepfun.ai/v1
# Optional voice provider env fallback. Fish realtime TTS also needs a Fish
# reference_id/voice ID saved in Voice Settings or supplied by the request.
FISH_AUDIO_API_KEY=
INWORLD_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
ASYNC_API_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=

# Optional model catalog/registry maintenance.
BATSHIT_MODEL_CATALOG_URL=https://api.batshit.ai/registry/catalog.json
ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY=
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN=

# Optional n8n integration.
# Default: connect Docker Batshit to a host n8n at http://host.docker.internal:5678.
# The normal `./start-docker.sh` path does not start n8n. If you explicitly run
# `./start-docker.sh --profile n8n`, the launcher rewrites N8N_API_URL to
# http://n8n:5678 when it still has the default host-managed value.
# When the optional n8n profile is used, Batshit rewrites callback URLs so n8n
# calls the app over the Compose network instead of browser-only localhost.
BATSHIT_N8N_CALLBACK_BASE_URL=http://app:3000
# Current official n8n Native Tools use the scoped native-tool token Batshit
# sends in each webhook payload. Older/custom service-token workflows must use
# this Docker instance's BATSHIT_TOKEN when they call Batshit directly.
# The optional n8n profile now uses the official pinned n8n image by default.
# Update n8n and runners together.
N8N_BASE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/n8n-io/n8n:2.22.1
N8N_RUNNERS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/n8n-io/runners:2.22.1
# Optional: defaults to BATSHIT_TOKEN when blank. Set a separate long token if
# you want n8n's task-runner broker to use a different internal secret.
N8N_RUNNERS_AUTH_TOKEN=
GENERIC_TIMEZONE=America/New_York
TZ=America/New_York
# Host/browser-facing URLs for the optional Docker n8n profile. These should use the
# published host port, not the internal Compose port, when
# BATSHIT_DOCKER_N8N_PORT is changed. Use http://127.0.0.1:<port> instead of
# localhost when you want this n8n profile's cookies isolated from another local n8n.
N8N_EDITOR_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5678
WEBHOOK_URL=http://localhost:5678/
N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=http://localhost:5678/webhook
# Batshit's app container should use the URL it can reach server-side.
# - Existing host-managed n8n: http://host.docker.internal:5678
# - Optional Docker n8n profile: http://n8n:5678
# `./start-docker.sh --profile n8n` rewrites this to http://n8n:5678 when it
# still has a default host-managed n8n URL. Direct Compose users should set it
# manually when enabling the optional n8n profile.
# Optional: Batshit can also store n8n API URL/key values in Settings -> API
# Keys. These values are for Batshit-side n8n API/MCP features, not Docker MCP
# Gateway auth.
N8N_API_URL=http://host.docker.internal:5678
N8N_API_KEY=
N8N_UI_EMAIL=
N8N_UI_PASSWORD=

# Internal Dev panel is off in public installs.
BATSHIT_ENABLE_INTERNAL_DEV_PANEL=0
BATSHIT_INTERNAL_DEV_PANEL_SECRET=
